So I took a bit of review on that ttyrec, and here are some thoughts.

The shield of reflection is always rustproof and corrodeproof (which
means that rust traps and acid-touch critters like ochre jellies will
never affect it), but can be deteriorated by destroy armor.  A confused
scroll of enchant armor should repair any damage on it just like it does
for other pieces of armor.

Your dwarvish iron helm started out "thoroughly rusty", so that getting 
toasted shouldn't be too surprising since any random shot can pretty 
much do it in -- and it's vulnerable to rust traps, rust monsters, and 
swimming.  I didn't see the jumping boots, though I didn't search all 
the ttyrecs, just the most recent one.  All things considered though,
I'd keep in mind that repairing damage _also_ restores fooproofing;
which can be a big difference when there are a lot of fire traps and 
rust traps around.

I can say this; I probably would _not_ have tried to melee the high
priest and both Rodneys all at the same time, and once leaving the
sanctum with a 'very deteriorated' shield I might have spent some time
digging for stuff to fix it.  (six levels later, you discovered why i
would have; in the middle of a fight is no time to have to take off
something like reflection to try to save it.  Getting hit four times in
a row is extremely unlikely; getting hit twice in a few turns is not.)

I also might have considered biting the bullet after the third level of
deterioration hit (putting the shield's existence at risk), taken the
shield off, left the Amulet behind, and dug down to try to obtain 
something to repair stuff with.  Or just to get space and time to do the
repair itself.

